"Grol nuktauru! Trort ugga!" At first, Doyle's voice trembles, but then he pulls himself together and pronounces this gibberish quite menacingly. You don't know what that means, but you feel that it takes effect upon the savages. 
You bring the torch to the lighter; bright fire blazes up, illuminating frightened painted faces. One of the natives tries to look brave. He has a high headwear of motley bird feathers; evidently, this is the chief of the tribe or the shaman.